<!--
Types which only the instance nodes reach, besides a declaration (opcua/instance-coverage).
- AlphaType declares a mandatory child "Unit" of UnitType, which defines a mandatory variable "Count". The instance's
  Unit uses UnitSubType, which adds a mandatory variable "Extra" of its own; the instance lacks Extra. UnitType's
  shape cannot report that, so UnitSubType needs a shape of its own.
- The instance organizes (Organizes) an object "Zeta" of ZetaType, which no type references. ZetaType defines a
  mandatory variable "Level"; the instance's Zeta lacks it.
- The instance also organizes "Misc", a plain BaseObjectType object: BaseObjectType defines no member, so no shape is
  written for it.
-->

